cartridge "SANTA'S BUSY DAY/G.TREPAL/1985"

' SANTA'S BUSY DAY
' A ColecoVision game based on "Santa's Busy Day" by George Trepal, Ahoy!
' December 1985 (Commodore 64: a BASIC loader that POKEs a Santa sprite and
' a machine-language game to $C000, started with SYS 49160). Made for Amy
' Studio by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic), 2026, in Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' The game: Santa is lost in a huge snowy maze strewn with gifts. Steer him
' through it and pick up the gifts before his time runs out. Santa keeps
' walking in the last direction you pushed; walking into a wall hurts
' (OUCH!), costs time and bounces him back. Two hearts hidden in the maze
' fill the time bar again. EASY: Santa stops when the stick is let go.
'
' From the original (orig/santa-ml.dis, the machine code read by hand): a
' perfect maze made by a random depth-first walk that keeps its way back
' in the cells themselves; the corridors and walls drawn three times as
' big as the maze grid, in a window that follows Santa; gifts and two
' hearts dropped at random; in REGULAR Santa keeps going in the last
' direction pushed, in EASY he moves only while the stick is held; a wall
' hit shows OUCH, costs a slice of the time bar and turns Santa round; a
' heart refills the bar; the game ends when the bar runs out or when
' enough gifts are collected (200 of the 210 dropped in the C64 version);
' the score is the number of gifts.
'
' Liberties: the maze is 12 x 26 cells (the C64's was 19 x 40; a byte a
' cell must fit in the ColecoVision's 1 KB of RAM), with 2-tile corridors
' and 1-tile walls (the C64's were 3 and 3) so Santa is a 16 x 16 sprite
' that walks smoothly, 2 pixels a frame; one gift per cell, 110 dropped
' and 100 needed (the C64 scattered 210 single characters and wanted 200);
' Santa turns only at cell centres, a push is remembered until the next
' turning (the C64 read the stick every step), and he can turn round at
' any time; the window jumps by three cells when Santa nears its edge
' (the C64 scrolled the screen every step); in EASY a wall stops Santa
' without the OUCH and its cost (on the C64 holding the stick into a wall
' kept hitting it); the time bar shows the time LEFT and turns red near
' the end, with a warning beep (the C64 filled a bar with time used);
' sounds for gifts and hearts, a jingle for the start, the end and a win;
' a title with a menu (EASY / REGULAR / CREDITS) instead of the E/R
' prompt, and the best score of the session.
'
' Controls: controller 1 (or 2): the stick walks Santa. On the title, up
' and down choose, a button chooses.
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128; the
' frame loop is protected from the NMI; screens drawn with the NMI off
' after a wait, display off. Music first in the sound table, effects after;
' the title tune (Deck the Halls, traditional) is played once. Random numbers
' from the built-in random().
'
' Workarounds for Amy bugs 25 (sprite count), 36 (random-half-range) removed 2026-11-01.

